# ── Why there is no .md rule here ────────────────────────────────────────────
# TESTED AND DISPROVEN 2026-08-06. Both "/*.md /404.html 404" and exact-filename
# rules ("/STATE.md /404.html 404") were deployed and NEITHER fired — /STATE.md
# kept returning 200. In the same deploy, "/ai-readiness / 301" worked, and the
# identical "/*.md" wildcard in _headers DID apply (X-Robots-Tag is live on all
# three docs). Same syntax, same deploy: headers matched, redirects did not.
#
# Conclusion: on Cloudflare Pages, static assets take precedence over _redirects.
# _redirects is routing for paths that DO NOT EXIST. It is not access control and
# cannot hide a file that is deployed.
#
# The docs are currently noindex/nofollow/noarchive via _headers but still
# fetchable. Closing that needs one of: a Pages Function, publishing from a build
# directory, or not committing operational docs into a deploy root at all.
# See playbook ARCHITECTURE.md, "Deploy roots are public".
